* ibufhalf: an instruction buffer answers for the half of its block that has
* come in, and only for that half.  A block is 32 words and is fetched in
* two halves, the one with the wanted parcel first; the four buffers are
* filled in rotation.
*   - Block 400 is fetched ahead as the jump at the end of block 340 is
*     reached, its first half first.  The jump goes to its second half,
*     which is still to come.  The buffer held block 200 before, whose
*     second half (words 220-223) is A7 A7+1.
*   - Block 440 is entered in its second half, which is fetched first, and
*     jumps back at once into its first half.  The buffer held block 240
*     before, which has A7 A7+1 where the first half of 440 has its code.
* Results: word 6000 = A5 (4), 6001 = A6 (2), 6002 = A7 (0).
         INCLUDE "rt_direct.cal"
         TBEGIN
         A5        0
         A6        0
         A7        0
         J         BK1
         ORG       220
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         ORG       240
BK1      J         BK2
         ORG       244
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         A7        A7+1
         ORG       300
BK2      J         BK3
         ORG       340
BK3      PASS
         PASS
